#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133592 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133783 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f260476d-35d0-504a-9e0a-86f7fb0049bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/id #uuid "1ad2672a-5773-5f2e-ab81-64e51ab4a7e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5570" :question/problem "Let ![](images/8a/8a460dfb89b0d2e9c1e197aa212f494971df1c36822117fb4b1271f5608d1d1a.png) and ![](images/a1/a172f54b0dc879c2363cfd2818fc79614d68662def6dd56b0ac9aec8fdbca1a5.png) Find the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{b}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{b}\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 9+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4+9+0-1}{4+1+0+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/id #uuid "2031cdd7-c43e-509c-8bb2-4d7362914e7b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5571" :question/problem "Let ![](images/fb/fb060fbc7ac20ff3b739a7c8958b4977e72abd31679c098973395db99fb6f78e.png) and ![](images/7a/7a20f39cb1c7c36a01e9d7d4dcd8cbe619c8cffacb57bc2bf42b8d46ce53bb5b.png) If $\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{y} + \\mathbf{z},$ where $\\mathbf{y} \\in \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ and $\\mathbf{z} \\perp \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\},$ then find $\\mathbf{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "A diagram of the situation is provided below:\n\n![](images/d8/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+0-2}{1+1+0+1}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}a \\\\  & =2a \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\mathbf{y} \\in \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ and $\\mathbf{z} \\perp \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\},$ as shown in the picture above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133785 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "5168f07e-4a22-5e0c-a612-e5c6f77f99eb" :question/math-academy-id "e-5572" :question/problem "Given the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the solution space of the system.\n![](images/37/37beee87c5b5bd6350bd2c0f6353b61b1cfd321449a96b8b66aac99584d459bb.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, $x_3$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get $x_2=4x_3.$ \nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain  \n\n$$\nx_1+4x_3+4x_3= 0\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx_1=-8x_3.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n![](images/49/4995b9959cbb8a412fe0ed6198bfa9a82bcda40cd388c4759589e060ec16de1e.png)\nConsequently, ![](images/23/232c58060c7ba67f66564e8f8667fe67a84f6ef886a1c56e2d042224ace9b4db.png) is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot (-8)+20\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1}{{(-8)}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{80+80+2}{64+16+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{162}{81}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133783 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f260476d-35d0-504a-9e0a-86f7fb0049bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00d5cc05-8499-57d3-b199-8e9a42a98221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269266} {:answer/id #uuid "1f9c3808-2157-5a66-90ff-9dc1609fca72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269533} {:answer/id #uuid "28bcee23-cd7e-59ab-b7cb-c0b1f222cb2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269635} {:answer/id #uuid "515f6dfa-1315-5132-b349-d3416447ab14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269996} {:answer/id #uuid "80a7d2f7-8510-54ed-9e26-519b2499409f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "515f6dfa-1315-5132-b349-d3416447ab14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269996} :answer-field/id #uuid "06d2f08a-4b4b-5b68-9a10-5ca42b5019a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7834509e-bd58-562a-9a2d-62496aca90f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-140114" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 8+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 10+2\\cdot 6}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{8+4-10+12}{1+1+1+4}b \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{7}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133783 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f260476d-35d0-504a-9e0a-86f7fb0049bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137079bc-1bf5-5584-937d-d91bc356f75d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269440} {:answer/id #uuid "2d61928e-0505-52e9-81cd-b5c7e1b2649e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269677} {:answer/id #uuid "44be6de1-7a1c-590d-b2b5-b419f0912d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269897} {:answer/id #uuid "b134bb6d-96cc-5baf-b399-5f1de5630e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270852} {:answer/id #uuid "b329c5d3-06f2-5e7e-8728-d1c7c202b545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d61928e-0505-52e9-81cd-b5c7e1b2649e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269677} :answer-field/id #uuid "983e6a8c-b20f-5d59-bc53-704f570ae0bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "764c79d6-0fb3-5c87-b4f5-38259f6c25dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-140115" :question/problem "Let $b=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 30 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}.$" :question/worked-solution "The vector projection of $b$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 12+(-1)\\cdot 30+0\\cdot 12+1\\cdot 24}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{12-30+0+24}{1+1+0+1}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}a \\\\  & =2a \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d587d0a-6ccd-5121-922b-75382faedfc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269510} {:answer/id #uuid "4b314729-0bd7-51bd-a0b8-51e6ac8592a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269946} {:answer/id #uuid "54f81c45-458b-541f-a41f-2e3f698557e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270024} {:answer/id #uuid "60a023c5-14a4-551c-9d4d-5d31ed9755bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270122} {:answer/id #uuid "e93fc3bd-07d9-5eca-9a15-ff0c19979237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d587d0a-6ccd-5121-922b-75382faedfc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269510} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab7c422b-7891-5a24-ace9-13b54a2c0dd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43c24ceb-8e96-51b5-b286-43fb903b1541" :question/math-academy-id "q-140116" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $x$ and $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by $‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}{b}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot (-2)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{6+4+2}{4+1+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-4)^{2}+(4-2)^{2}+(-2-(-2))^{2}+(-2-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+0+4} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef772d27-a54c-5362-adfe-f41ae7b23dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398433} {:answer/id #uuid "a557db17-2b18-5b72-9311-1df4e238f75d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398434} {:answer/id #uuid "71b74f4c-2b14-5f0c-9aa3-db59d3b3ef3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398435} {:answer/id #uuid "8642137f-d66c-5a2c-ae0a-4ef5266bcf18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398436} {:answer/id #uuid "34b99926-5586-5bc7-ba1f-bc66c66e6e8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef772d27-a54c-5362-adfe-f41ae7b23dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398433} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74f3682-41ce-5a31-9b35-9471ffa05fed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d62d6869-fd0d-50a4-9c77-6fb492970304" :question/math-academy-id "q-140117" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d8/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot (-5)+6\\cdot 5+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+30+6+4}{4+36+4+16}a \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{60}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ddd3f62-1e8c-5f20-8e93-a2945985e065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324752} {:answer/id #uuid "63c82cf6-2fd6-5c93-ab3c-ba60ed211320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324798} {:answer/id #uuid "904b53b6-3f3a-5655-a771-938b662294a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325198} {:answer/id #uuid "944c2eb8-b585-5b90-a0cb-4b41d812753f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325235} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ab2ab2-3f7b-5481-aece-6220e2d37451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "904b53b6-3f3a-5655-a771-938b662294a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325198} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3b18b52-c46f-59cc-a46f-8b8a70fa4198" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "093d7617-4a17-5d9a-be95-4758456c60a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-39712" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d8/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 12+6\\cdot 6+(-6)\\cdot (-6)+2\\cdot 12}{{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{24+36+36+24}{4+36+36+4}a \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{80}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133785 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "138cac23-370e-5839-a092-017a89719e39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417842} {:answer/id #uuid "274b7a59-8d6d-5f0d-a5bb-67d68e47b623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}50 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 75\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417845} {:answer/id #uuid "322e7a13-5d76-5091-9b4c-c0404f19e1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417847} {:answer/id #uuid "5a72aa28-97b8-5365-be9f-89839b7d4d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417851} {:answer/id #uuid "9859e5a1-f120-56a8-a412-5c766fcc01c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{7} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{7} \\\\ \\frac{15}{7}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a72aa28-97b8-5365-be9f-89839b7d4d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417851} :answer-field/id #uuid "84ea1ef5-c4c4-50df-8964-7eae36e54128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3a5d3d6c-a506-54c8-bf1d-2c93ad742095" :question/math-academy-id "q-39718" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3})=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{6}{5}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot 6+(-15)\\cdot 3+28\\cdot 5}{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{5}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-60-45+140}{36+9+25}b \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{70}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f4697c1-ec55-5d26-a4f9-52ee4b8db881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324113} {:answer/id #uuid "84e9d18f-6b68-5f06-9f20-a0d363dae9e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325093} {:answer/id #uuid "8f50a969-fbe8-5fd7-9bae-c1a0508f3520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325186} {:answer/id #uuid "95ec8124-7ed3-5587-a819-e42cdd9fb6eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325250} {:answer/id #uuid "cb67ab6f-d399-58d9-b7d6-2150a80d04f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f50a969-fbe8-5fd7-9bae-c1a0508f3520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325186} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e05148d-86cd-5a75-9827-8b82aa66eb70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8506ae4c-a408-5064-a44b-7c4e253ac4df" :question/math-academy-id "q-40409" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $x$ and $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by $‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}{b}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-4)+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 3}{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\text{ }\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{6+0+6+0}{9+0+9+0}\\text{ }\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ }\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+((-4)-0)^{2}+((-2)-(-2))^{2}+(3-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+0+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133785 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe651140-b1a7-53a9-be39-625f78f54806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394135} {:answer/id #uuid "0306defa-09b7-53c6-8452-4673eb962945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394136} {:answer/id #uuid "868aeae6-feb8-580a-b125-c852175f477e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394137} {:answer/id #uuid "d40d5338-efdc-5c78-a85b-7d978d2b3564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394138} {:answer/id #uuid "3943a917-5fdc-5619-ae8d-31464ae3c9b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe651140-b1a7-53a9-be39-625f78f54806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394135} :answer-field/id #uuid "d253c50a-a61f-5f25-9a5a-b2a79e339ce2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f7628d96-7413-59a8-b813-69718d9f2735" :question/math-academy-id "q-81196" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3}b \\\\  & =4b \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133785 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43b8e169-1542-57e2-b61e-4578bd89d307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349061} {:answer/id #uuid "97f968d3-d009-5441-a771-fb094e810909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349808} {:answer/id #uuid "a5eb7c71-d1a4-5cfc-a8c7-37f0c3d79020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349925} {:answer/id #uuid "c943b145-f4b1-52fe-b30e-30e008493d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350218} {:answer/id #uuid "f7885772-3dd4-5872-80ac-0681418d107d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97f968d3-d009-5441-a771-fb094e810909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349808} :answer-field/id #uuid "d84d7b27-f4f1-5d53-a4a3-9cd78438ca6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e4dfd3ff-f06c-510f-a866-eb14bbbfe76a" :question/math-academy-id "q-81201" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of  linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{10}b \\\\  & =b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "036fc91b-555a-5bcf-a35b-9f142e50406f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351599} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc325d5-c26f-5c6d-969f-fb0017854f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351815} {:answer/id #uuid "e4713ebf-6def-5cb1-9c8f-62455e04773b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353562} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c7ca8a-3389-5fbe-9881-4e0716e75eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353706} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f50dc7-a326-5a6f-97a9-3d0f5cb52102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4713ebf-6def-5cb1-9c8f-62455e04773b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353562} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaa4125b-6e38-5ac0-a313-e9cea2ec6466" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "257d56b8-a016-5f07-afca-c70db1a86155" :question/math-academy-id "q-86733" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d8/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 4}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3+2+(-2)+12}{1+4+1+9}a \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{15}a \\\\  & =a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
